ce and the state  dependents together suggested to us that  global stimulation may be a feasible  treatment option that was worth further  exploration and may even  be necessary  so in addition to the clinical mapping  we also did biomarker exploration during  this period so we had the patient  perform 335 vas scales of depression  anxiety over the 10 days which we used  to define two symptoms severity states a  low and a high symptom severity state  and we identified the 15 minutes of  resting state  ing activity that coincided with the  clinical measures where one of these two  states was present  and then we identified the spectral  activity features that discriminated the  high and low symptom states using two  different cross-validated supervised  machine learning models at different  spatial resolutions  in the first model which is shown on the  top here  spectral power was averaged across all  contacts within a brain region so it was  a region level model and here we found  that gamma power in bilateral amygdala  right ofc left subject of cingulate and  right hippocampus had high state  discriminative potential  in our second model  the feature set was defined by spectral  power for each electrode contact so  across including across all the brain  regions and that allowed us to account  for intra-regional variability due to  the electrode positioning  and with this model we found bilateral  amygdala gamma power alone was actually  sufficient for detecting the high  symptom  it was simpler than we initially  anticipated  so it suggests that amygdala gamma power  is a biomarker of the highly depressed  state in this individual  so we found the ventral capsule was a  brain site where stimulation led to  consistent improvement in symptoms and  amygdala was the site of the biomarker  activity we next examine the  connectivity across the cortical limbic  network to determine whether the ventral  capsule and amygdalin nodes constituted  a structurally and functionally  connected subnetwork so that ventral  capsule stimulation directly influenced  amygdala biomarker activity and to us  this provided  further justification for selection of  these sites for the placement of the  sensing and stimulation leads  so to examine the effective network  connectivity we used to vote potential  mapping ep mapping so we delivered  single pulses in one region and looked  at the evo potential in a distant  contact and then we identified the n1  and then to peak deflection magnitude  using standard approaches  um  oh and so that's what i'm showing here  in this first circle plot in a  um it's the directed graph for the n1  and the percent circumference here  indicates the strength of the connection  between any two of the brain regions  and the color here  indicates the starting location so for  the ventral capsule you can see the  yellow connections  pointing towards the hippocampus in  black  high activity strength and the direction  was then quantified by calculating the  weighted in degree weighted in degree is  the weighted sum of significant  connections pointing towards a node and  we  calculated the out degree which is the  weighted sum of connections pointing  away from the node  and  we did this in order to identify the  most influential hubs across this  network and  interestingly we found that the bento  capsule had the highest weighted out  degree suggesting it has strong  connections to other brain regions and  the amygdala and hippocampus had the  highest weighted in degree suggesting  they received connections from many  other brain regions and this is  consistent with what we might  want for a stimulation and sensing  selection and sites for deep brain  stimulation  so we then examine the axonal fiber  tracts that might mediate this effect of  connectivity using dti and this was  aided by one of our collaborators  in neuroradiology leo sugru and we found  that there was also dense structural  connectivity between the right ven