dy and we use the dti that i  just showed you in planning of this  surgery so that the contacts interface  with those two fiber tracks the strea  terminolus and the antipresent solaris  and then we were able we planned it out  that way and then we were able to  successfully replicate the positioning  of the of the contacts we were looking  for  we then assessed whether we could also  replicate the clinical effect of the  ventral capsule stimulation that we saw  in mapping studies and we found that at  the expected context based on anatomy we  again saw acute symptom improvement  across the majority of trials um and the  patient describes it as pleasurable and  energizing just as in stage one and in  fact we saw the opposite effect with  stimulation amygdala which  was a  control  you can see that stimulating there made  her symptoms generally worse  so furthermore in closed loop  stimulation in addition to the frequency  and pulse width and current amplitude we  also have to consider the burst duration  of stimulation as well  so to do this we tested the clinical  effects of intermittent stimulation  at different stimulation burst durations  over a 15 and 30 minute period  and we found that just six seconds of  intermittent stimulation at one milliamp  was clinically effective  and with something that was important to  us it was below the patient's perceptual  threshold meaning that she couldn't  detect you know these on off state  transitions  which we didn't want because we didn't  want her to go through her day feeling  this the stimulation go on and off  in  we also found that we were able to  replicate the symptom specific biomarker  for the closed loop control so we use  the neuropathy system telemetry wand to  stream eco on in the lab and then we  recorded 10 minute trials of continuous  and medical activity while the patient  engaged in naturalistic activities  this might include looking at her social  media talking to family on the phone  watching clips of 