opped below 10  remission  within several months  and she remains in remission today so  it's been um almost two years at this  point that she  when she first  got had her first surgery  so to further then test whether the  closed-loop algorithm triggered  stimulation in a manner linked to the  patient's symptoms and not randomly we  examined then the relationship between  a morning symptom severity rating that  she did at home  and the daily detection count over the  two-month period and we used dynamic  time warping so we could non-linearly  align this daily symptom severity and  biomarker detection count time traces  and you can see here how high they are  this is the purple and the gray lines we  found that the fluctuation daily  symptoms was significantly associated  with the fluctuation in number of  biomarker events detected by the device  and this suggests that  you know it detects change in symptoms  severity  better than chance rather than just  stimulating intermittently  so in summary we replicated the effects  of the mapping study with the neuropaste  device the effects of the clinical  response to the ventral capsule  stimulation was positive and energizing  and amygdala gamma power was again found  to be predictive of the symptom severity  state  and as i mentioned this patient's  depression is currently in remission  she's  doing really well she started driving  again after not driving for a lot of  years  she's taking computer programming  classes python classes and engaged  in going to school with  a goal of moving back into the workforce  so it's really  been amazing to watch this transition in  her life  oh i can okay so  all right so we have a lot of work left  to do  we don't yet know how variable these  findings will be across individuals we  have implanted a couple of additional  subjects at this point in different  brain locations so we don't think the  same biomarker and treatment site is is  going to be in the same across all our  patients